   - *Teachable Moment*: While recognizing that dynamically allocated memories require releasing after use prevents leaks — explicitly mentioning `free` correctly alongside malloc highlights mastery here! "When we allocate memory with 'malloc', it's crucial afterwards to ensure no unused resources linger by freeing what was reserved via free(ptr). This frees up space previously occupied."
